hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1132","Chapter on freeing slaves of the polytheists who accept Islam, 1172 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Rib'i, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Two slaves of the people of Mecca went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah before the truce and accepted Islam. Their masters among the people of Mecca sent concerning them: By Allah, O Muhammad, they did not come out to you out of desire for your religion; they came out only fleeing from slavery. Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; return them to them. He grew angry and said: I do not see you, O company of Quraysh, desisting until Allah sends against you one who will strike your necks for this religion. He refused to return them and said: They are Allah's freedmen."
